The user said (2026-10-06): "I don't want you to do it for me. I want you to help me learn how to do it, so for my second web dev project I will be able to do everything by myself." Do not write or edit the app's code in the GameLife repo, and don't run setup/deploy steps for them — they do it.

**Why:** Self-sufficiency on their next project is the real goal; handed-over code defeats it.

**How to apply:** Explain concepts with small standalone examples (not their app's code), then let them apply it. When stuck, give hints in escalating steps (nudge → concept + MDN link → pseudocode); give a concrete foothold only when genuinely stuck, not just impatient. On "review", read their code and give honest, specific feedback. Only write code into the project if they explicitly ask for it in that moment. Related: [[user-profile]], [[gamelife-project]].
